# Repository Patterns and Data Access

## Overview
The repository layer handles all data access operations using JPA repositories, custom repositories, and JOOQ for complex queries. This layer provides a clean abstraction over the database and implements optimized query patterns.

## Repository Types

### 1. JPA Repositories
Located in `repositories/` package, extend `JpaRepository` for basic CRUD operations:

```java
@Repository
public interface TimesheetRepository extends JpaRepository<Timesheet, Integer> {
    
    // Basic query methods
    List<Timesheet> findByCandidateId(Integer candidateId);
    List<Timesheet> findByJobIdAndStatus(Integer jobId, String status);
    Optional<Timesheet> findByIdAndAccountId(Integer id, Integer accountId);
    
    // Custom queries with @Query
    @Query("SELECT t FROM Timesheet t WHERE t.candidateId = :candidateId AND t.status = :status")
    List<Timesheet> findTimesheetsByCandidateAndStatus(@Param("candidateId") Integer candidateId, 
                                                      @Param("status") String status);
    
    // Entity graph to avoid N+1 problems
    @EntityGraph(attributePaths = {"candidate", "job"})
    @Query("SELECT t FROM Timesheet t WHERE t.id IN :ids")
    List<Timesheet> findByIdsWithRelatedEntities(@Param("ids") List<Integer> ids);
}
```

### 2. Custom Repositories
Located in `dao/` package, implement complex business logic:

```java
@Repository
public class TimesheetDao {
    
    private final JooqDslContextTarget jooqDslContextTarget;
    private final TimesheetRepository timesheetRepository;
    
    public TimesheetDao(JooqDslContextTarget jooqDslContextTarget, 
                       TimesheetRepository timesheetRepository) {
        this.jooqDslContextTarget = jooqDslContextTarget;
        this.timesheetRepository = timesheetRepository;
    }
    
    // Complex queries using JOOQ
    public List<TimesheetPermissionDataDto> findTimesheetPermissionData(List<Integer> timesheetIds, 
                                                                       Integer accountId) {
        return jooqDslContextTarget.getDslContext()
            .select(Tables.TIMESHEET.ID, Tables.TIMESHEET.CANDIDATE_ID, Tables.TIMESHEET.JOB_ID)
            .from(Tables.TIMESHEET)
            .where(Tables.TIMESHEET.ID.in(timesheetIds))
            .and(Tables.TIMESHEET.ACCOUNT_ID.eq(accountId))
            .fetchInto(TimesheetPermissionDataDto.class);
    }
}
```

### 3. JOOQ Integration
For complex SQL queries and dynamic query building:

```java
@Component
public class SortingQueryBuilder {
    
    public SelectConditionStep<Record> buildSearchQuery(SearchRequestBodyDto searchRequest) {
        SelectConditionStep<Record> query = jooqDslContextTarget.getDslContext()
            .select()
            .from(Tables.TIMESHEET)
            .where(Tables.TIMESHEET.ACCOUNT_ID.eq(accountId));
            
        // Add search conditions
        if (searchRequest.getName() != null) {
            query = query.and(Tables.TIMESHEET.NAME.like("%" + searchRequest.getName() + "%"));
        }
        
        // Add sorting
        if (searchRequest.getSortBy() != null) {
            query = query.orderBy(buildSortField(searchRequest.getSortBy(), searchRequest.getSortDirection()));
        }
        
        return query;
    }
}
```

## Query Optimization Patterns

### 1. Entity Graph for Eager Loading
```java
@Repository
public interface TimesheetRepository extends JpaRepository<Timesheet, Integer> {
    
    // Use EntityGraph to load related entities in single query
    @EntityGraph(attributePaths = {"candidate", "job", "timeLogs"})
    @Query("SELECT t FROM Timesheet t WHERE t.id = :id")
    Optional<Timesheet> findByIdWithRelatedEntities(@Param("id") Integer id);
    
    // Load multiple entities with relationships
    @EntityGraph(attributePaths = {"candidate", "job"})
    @Query("SELECT t FROM Timesheet t WHERE t.id IN :ids")
    List<Timesheet> findByIdsWithRelatedEntities(@Param("ids") List<Integer> ids);
}
```

### 2. Bulk Operations
```java
@Repository
public interface TimesheetRepository extends JpaRepository<Timesheet, Integer> {
    
    // Batch save for performance
    @Transactional
    default List<Timesheet> saveAllBatch(List<Timesheet> timesheets) {
        List<Timesheet> saved = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int i = 0; i < timesheets.size(); i++) {
            saved.add(save(timesheets.get(i)));
            if (i % 50 == 0) {
                flush(); // Flush every 50 entities
            }
        }
        return saved;
    }
    
    // Bulk update
    @Modifying
    @Query("UPDATE Timesheet t SET t.status = :status WHERE t.id IN :ids")
    int updateStatusByIds(@Param("status") String status, @Param("ids") List<Integer> ids);
}
```

### 3. Projection Queries
```java
@Repository
public interface TimesheetRepository extends JpaRepository<Timesheet, Integer> {
    
