## Search and Filtering

### 1. Dynamic Search Queries
```java
@Component
public class TimesheetSearchRepository {
    
    public Page<Timesheet> searchTimesheets(SearchRequestBodyDto searchRequest, 
                                          PaginationRequestBodyDto pagination,
                                          Integer accountId) {
        
        SelectConditionStep<Record> query = jooqDslContextTarget.getDslContext()
            .selectFrom(Tables.TIMESHEET)
            .where(Tables.TIMESHEET.ACCOUNT_ID.eq(accountId));
            
        // Add search filters
        if (searchRequest.getName() != null) {
            query = query.and(Tables.TIMESHEET.NAME.like("%" + searchRequest.getName() + "%"));
        }
        
        if (searchRequest.getStatus() != null) {
            query = query.and(Tables.TIMESHEET.STATUS.eq(searchRequest.getStatus()));
        }
        
        if (searchRequest.getCandidateId() != null) {
            query = query.and(Tables.TIMESHEET.CANDIDATE_ID.eq(searchRequest.getCandidateId()));
        }
        
        if (searchRequest.getJobId() != null) {
            query = query.and(Tables.TIMESHEET.JOB_ID.eq(searchRequest.getJobId()));
        }
        
        // Add date range filters
        if (searchRequest.getDateFrom() != null) {
            query = query.and(Tables.TIMESHEET.DATE.goe(searchRequest.getDateFrom()));
        }
        
        if (searchRequest.getDateTo() != null) {
            query = query.and(Tables.TIMESHEET.DATE.loe(searchRequest.getDateTo()));
        }
        
        // Add sorting
        if (pagination.getSortBy() != null) {
            query = query.orderBy(buildSortField(pagination.getSortBy(), pagination.getSortDirection()));
        }
        
        // Add pagination
        int offset = (pagination.getPage() - 1) * pagination.getSize();
        query = query.limit(pagination.getSize()).offset(offset);
        
        return executeQueryWithPagination(query, pagination);
    }
}
```

### 2. Sorting Query Builder
```java
@Component
public class SortingQueryBuilder {
    
    private SortField<?> buildSortField(String sortBy, String sortDirection) {
        Field<?> field = getFieldByName(sortBy);
        return sortDirection.equalsIgnoreCase("DESC") ? field.desc() : field.asc();
    }
    
    private Field<?> getFieldByName(String fieldName) {
        switch (fieldName.toLowerCase()) {
            case "name": return Tables.TIMESHEET.NAME;
            case "status": return Tables.TIMESHEET.STATUS;
            case "date": return Tables.TIMESHEET.DATE;
            case "created_at": return Tables.TIMESHEET.CREATED_AT;
            default: return Tables.TIMESHEET.ID;
        }
    }
}
```

## Transaction Management

### 1. Service-Level Transactions
```java
@Service
@Transactional
public class TimesheetService {
    
    @Transactional(readOnly = true)
    public List<Timesheet> findTimesheetsByCandidate(Integer candidateId) {
        return timesheetRepository.findByCandidateId(candidateId);
    }
    
    @Transactional
    public Timesheet createTimesheet(TimesheetRequestDto request) {
        // Create timesheet
        Timesheet timesheet = new Timesheet();
        timesheet.setName(request.name());
        timesheet.setCandidateId(request.candidateId());
        timesheet.setJobId(request.jobId());
        
        Timesheet savedTimesheet = timesheetRepository.save(timesheet);
        
        // Create related time logs
        if (request.timeLogs() != null) {
            List<TimeLog> timeLogs = request.timeLogs().stream()
                .map(this::createTimeLog)
                .toList();
            timeLogRepository.saveAll(timeLogs);
        }
        
        return savedTimesheet;
    }
}
```

### 2. Repository-Level Transactions
```java
@Repository
public class TimesheetDao {
    
    @Transactional
    public void bulkUpdateStatus(List<Integer> timesheetIds, String status) {
        // Use JOOQ for bulk update
        jooqDslContextTarget.getDslContext()
            .update(Tables.TIMESHEET)
            .set(Tables.TIMESHEET.STATUS, status)
            .set(Tables.TIMESHEET.UPDATED_AT, LocalDateTime.now())
            .where(Tables.TIMESHEET.ID.in(timesheetIds))
            .execute();
    }
}
```

## Error Handling

### 1. Repository Exception Handling
```java
@Repository
public class TimesheetRepository {
    
    public Optional<Timesheet> findByIdSafely(Integer id) {
        try {
            return findById(id);
        } catch (DataAccessException ex) {
            logger.error("Database error while finding timesheet with id: " + id, ex);
            throw new RepositoryException("Failed to find timesheet", ex);
        }
    }
    
    public List<Timesheet> saveAllSafely(List<Timesheet> timesheets) {
        try {
            return saveAll(timesheets);
        } catch (DataAccessException ex) {
            logger.error("Database error while saving timesheets", ex);
            throw new RepositoryException("Failed to save timesheets", ex);
        }
    }
}
```

## Best Practices

### 1. Query Optimization
- Use `@EntityGraph` to avoid N+1 problems
- Use projections to select only needed fields
- Use bulk operations for multiple records
- Use indexes on frequently queried fields

### 2. Transaction Management
- Use `@Transactional(readOnly = true)` for read operations
- Use `@Transactional` for write operations
- Keep transactions as short as possible
- Use appropriate isolation levels

### 3. Error Handling
- Catch and log database exceptions
- Throw custom exceptions with meaningful messages
- Use safe methods for critical operations
- Implement retry logic for transient failures

### 4. Performance
- Use pagination for large result sets
- Use caching for frequently accessed data
- Use batch operations for bulk updates
- Monitor query performance with logging



